Z||000004||fiero56||01-29-2000||03:01 PM||||I have two hydraulic floor jacks(the kind with a stick you pump). Other than that I use a pair of jackstands, and a complete set of tools. I was actually surprised when I went back into the house and looked at the clock. I started at 9:45pm,and I went in for the night after dropping the engine cradle at 11:55pm. I did the clutch replacement earier this morning, and all I have left is to hook everything back up.||||reg||10
Z||000005||Monkeyman||01-29-2000||07:31 PM||||Did you forget to tell us about the 6 hours when the power failed and you forgot to reset the clocks? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I've never had to drop the cradle (but I'll be finding out in a couple of months!) but that sounds like you really worked hard at it.  How long did it take you the 1st time?||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||01-29-2000||10:03 PM||||Took me two weeks to do the complete clutch job last time. But that involved many trips to Sears, Lowes, and Furrow. Plus, I broke the brand new slave I had bought, so I had to wait 4 days to get another. Not to mention cutting holes in the frame to get the cradle bolts free. Just a big mess. <P>But it finally caught up with me today. Today I pulled the tranny did the clutch swap, everything went fine. Then tried to reinstall the 80lb(?) tranny. I spent 5 hours this afternoon trying to get the input shaft to join the clutch disk. Will not go. My back hurt so much, I gave up for the day. Maybe tommorrow. No, I will finish tommorrow. My new flywheel shore is perty though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||01-30-2000||01:25 AM||||fiero56,<P>Something ain't right if you couldn't get it on in 5 hours! I assume you aligned the clutch? Right clutch (dia. and # teeth)? Right flywheel? <P>You may want to take pressure plate off and trial fit clutch disc on shaft and tranny to engine. Extra work, but you already 5 hrs invested...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||01-30-2000||06:25 AM||||fiero56--Furrows?  Isn't that a lumber yard?  What could you possible need with a lumber yard when working on a Fiero?  Oh, I know.  New wood for the gaskets, right?  Maybe a sheet of plywood to cover up the rear window that you broke out when you got pi**ed and the wrench "slipped"?||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||01-30-2000||03:43 PM||||Monkey:<BR>Your right Furrow's is a lumber place. I didn't get lumber there, but I remember having to go there to get something. Just can't remmeber what.<BR>I used the alignment tool. It is lined up properly. I thought about the input shaft not being compatible, but I used the alignment tool, and it fit the new disk as well as the one I took off. I think I just haven't been able to get everything perfectly aligned.<P>I didn't work 5 hours straight on this problem. An hour here, two there, 30min here... I'm on my way out the door to try again.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phaeton||01-30-2000||04:18 PM||||I'm really glad to hear it took five hours for the clutch.  No wait let me reprase that.  I'm glad it's not just me that can't get a clutch shaft through.  After I got all the 'hard' stuff done and just had to push the tranny back on the engine everything came to a dead stop.  It was like a jealous toyota owner had cursed the shop, four hours before I stopped for a breather.  Is this something that gets easier with practice or do random quantum fluctuations control the destiny of output shafts? No, really, it finally went in like it had butter on the shaft and I don't know why, I was pushing and twisting just the same as the first four hours but for some reason it slid right on.  Still looking for an inexpensive four speed lockup.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||01-30-2000||07:25 PM||||I went out, picked the tranny off the floor, shoved it in the bay, and it slid right on. Perfectly. Took, maybe 5 minutes to bolt it in place. I knew that was going to happen. I was glad it went in place, but not that I spent 5 hours yesterday with no pregress. I've taken a break for the game, but all will be in place soon.<P>The first time took me 15 minutes, just a little shoving and twisting and it went on. I don't think I will get enough practice putting a tranny on, to make the job any faster.||||reg||7
